-- title:
--   Ten coefficient identities for Klein's edge form under U
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero and let $\alpha,\beta,s\in K$. Four relations are assumed: `h1` asserts $\alpha\beta=-s$, `h2` asserts $2\alpha^{2}=-5-s$, `h3` asserts $2\beta^{2}=s-5$, and `h4` asserts $s^{2}=5$. (These are the relations satisfied by $\alpha=\zeta-\zeta^{4}$, $\beta=\zeta^{2}-\zeta^{3}$, $s=\zeta+\zeta^{4}-\zeta^{2}-\zeta^{3}$ for $\zeta$ a primitive fifth root of unity, but no such presentation is assumed: the elements are abstract and only the four displayed identities are available.)
--
--   The conclusion is a conjunction of ten equations between homogeneous expressions of total degree $30$ in $\alpha$ and $\beta$ with explicit integer coefficients. Write
--   $$E_{1}=-10005\beta^{30}+2001000\alpha^{2}\beta^{28}-85542750\alpha^{4}\beta^{26}-27733860\alpha^{5}\beta^{25}+1368684000\alpha^{6}\beta^{24}+462231000\alpha^{7}\beta^{23}-10179587250\alpha^{8}\beta^{22}-2509254000\alpha^{9}\beta^{21}+37271176275\alpha^{10}\beta^{20}+5645821500\alpha^{11}\beta^{19}-64632300000\alpha^{12}\beta^{18}-5332164750\alpha^{13}\beta^{17}+36355668750\alpha^{14}\beta^{16}+36355668750\alpha^{16}\beta^{14}+5332164750\alpha^{17}\beta^{13}-64632300000\alpha^{18}\beta^{12}-5645821500\alpha^{19}\beta^{11}+37271176275\alpha^{20}\beta^{10}+2509254000\alpha^{21}\beta^{9}-10179587250\alpha^{22}\beta^{8}-462231000\alpha^{23}\beta^{7}+1368684000\alpha^{24}\beta^{6}+27733860\alpha^{25}\beta^{5}-85542750\alpha^{26}\beta^{4}+2001000\alpha^{28}\beta^{2}-10005\alpha^{30},$$
--   $$E_{2}=200100\alpha\beta^{29}-19009500\alpha^{3}\beta^{27}+513256500\alpha^{5}\beta^{25}+92446200\alpha^{6}\beta^{24}-5816907000\alpha^{7}\beta^{23}-1254627000\alpha^{8}\beta^{22}+30894239400\alpha^{9}\beta^{21}+5645821500\alpha^{10}\beta^{20}-79293827100\alpha^{11}\beta^{19}-10664329500\alpha^{12}\beta^{18}+87253605000\alpha^{13}\beta^{17}+6204700800\alpha^{14}\beta^{16}+6204700800\alpha^{16}\beta^{14}-87253605000\alpha^{17}\beta^{13}-10664329500\alpha^{18}\beta^{12}+79293827100\alpha^{19}\beta^{11}+5645821500\alpha^{20}\beta^{10}-30894239400\alpha^{21}\beta^{9}-1254627000\alpha^{22}\beta^{8}+5816907000\alpha^{23}\beta^{7}+92446200\alpha^{24}\beta^{6}-513256500\alpha^{25}\beta^{5}+19009500\alpha^{27}\beta^{3}-200100\alpha^{29}\beta,$$
--   $$E_{3}=-1900950\alpha^{2}\beta^{28}+114057000\alpha^{4}\beta^{26}-2181340125\alpha^{6}\beta^{24}-250925400\alpha^{7}\beta^{23}+17353772550\alpha^{8}\beta^{22}+2822910750\alpha^{9}\beta^{21}-64632300000\alpha^{10}\beta^{20}-10664329500\alpha^{11}\beta^{19}+112352798325\alpha^{12}\beta^{18}+14348370600\alpha^{13}\beta^{17}-63016492500\alpha^{14}\beta^{16}-63016492500\alpha^{16}\beta^{14}-14348370600\alpha^{17}\beta^{13}+112352798325\alpha^{18}\beta^{12}+10664329500\alpha^{19}\beta^{11}-64632300000\alpha^{20}\beta^{10}-2822910750\alpha^{21}\beta^{9}+17353772550\alpha^{22}\beta^{8}+250925400\alpha^{23}\beta^{7}-2181340125\alpha^{24}\beta^{6}+114057000\alpha^{26}\beta^{4}-1900950\alpha^{28}\beta^{2},$$
--   $$E_{4}=11405700\alpha^{3}\beta^{27}-484742250\alpha^{5}\beta^{25}+6204700800\alpha^{7}\beta^{23}+564582150\alpha^{8}\beta^{22}-33931957500\alpha^{9}\beta^{21}-5332164750\alpha^{10}\beta^{20}+87253605000\alpha^{11}\beta^{19}+14348370600\alpha^{12}\beta^{18}-95904828450\alpha^{13}\beta^{17}-9694845000\alpha^{14}\beta^{16}-9694845000\alpha^{16}\beta^{14}+95904828450\alpha^{17}\beta^{13}+14348370600\alpha^{18}\beta^{12}-87253605000\alpha^{19}\beta^{11}-5332164750\alpha^{20}\beta^{10}+33931957500\alpha^{21}\beta^{9}+564582150\alpha^{22}\beta^{8}-6204700800\alpha^{23}\beta^{7}+484742250\alpha^{25}\beta^{5}-11405700\alpha^{27}\beta^{3},$$
--   $$E_{5}=-48474225\alpha^{4}\beta^{26}+1163381400\alpha^{6}\beta^{24}-9694845000\alpha^{8}\beta^{22}-1066432950\alpha^{9}\beta^{21}+36355668750\alpha^{10}\beta^{20}+6204700800\alpha^{11}\beta^{19}-63016492500\alpha^{12}\beta^{18}-9694845000\alpha^{13}\beta^{17}+35434658475\alpha^{14}\beta^{16}+35434658475\alpha^{16}\beta^{14}+9694845000\alpha^{17}\beta^{13}-63016492500\alpha^{18}\beta^{12}-6204700800\alpha^{19}\beta^{11}+36355668750\alpha^{20}\beta^{10}+1066432950\alpha^{21}\beta^{9}-9694845000\alpha^{22}\beta^{8}+1163381400\alpha^{24}\beta^{6}-48474225\alpha^{26}\beta^{4}.$$
--   The ten conjuncts, in the order in which they occur, are then: $E_{1}=-305328369140625$ (the right-hand side being $-10005\cdot 5^{15}$); $E_{2}=0$; $E_{3}=0$; $E_{4}=0$; $E_{5}=0$; $E_{5}=0$ again, the sixth conjunct repeating the fifth verbatim; $-E_{4}=0$, the seventh conjunct being the fourth with every coefficient negated; $E_{3}=0$ again, the eighth conjunct repeating the third verbatim; $-E_{2}=0$, the ninth conjunct being the second with every coefficient negated; and finally $E_{1}=-305328369140625$ again, the tenth conjunct repeating the first verbatim.
--
--   In each $E_{i}$ the monomial $\alpha^{15}\beta^{15}$ is absent, the coefficients of $\alpha^{a}\beta^{b}$ and $\alpha^{b}\beta^{a}$ agree when $a$ and $b$ are even, and they are opposite when $a$ and $b$ are odd.
--
--   These ten equations are the second block of the coefficient identities that express the covariance of Klein's binary edge form $T$ of degree $30$ under the half-turn $U=\tfrac1s\begin{pmatrix}-\alpha&\beta\\ \beta&\alpha\end{pmatrix}$ of the binary icosahedral group, stated as a finite polynomial certificate over any field of characteristic zero in terms of abstract $\alpha,\beta,s$ subject to the four relations. They are used by [`RubinSilverberg.kleinTHom_atomsU`](thm.html#RubinSilverberg.kleinTHom_atomsU), in the verification that $U$ is a symmetry of the Rubin–Silverberg datum underlying the family of elliptic curves with constant mod-$5$ representation.
